# nano-blog — permanent redirects
#
# The site has no previous address, so there is nothing to redirect yet. The
# specification forbids sending unknown old URLs to the home page, so this file
# stays empty of catch-all rules on purpose.
#
# When a published article's path changes, add one explicit 301 per moved URL:
#
#   /posts/old/path/  /posts/new/path/  301
#
# `content:validate` and `content:publish` both check this table for loops,
# chains, missing destinations and catch-all wildcards, so a rule added here
# cannot quietly break. See docs/WRITING.md section 6.1.
